title: Step definitions
section: Writing tests
desc: Write step definitions with Cucumber Expressions or regular expressions, use the context, and set timeouts and retries.
lede: A step definition connects a line of a scenario to code. Given, When and Then are interchangeable for matching, so use whichever reads best.
---
<h2>Your first step</h2>
<cb title="steps/basket.steps.ts">import { strict as assert } from 'node:assert';
import { Given, When, Then } from '@bddr/runtime';

Given('an empty basket', (ctx) => {
  ctx.state.set('lines', []);
});

When('I add {int} {string}', (ctx, qty: number, product: string) => {
  ctx.state.get<Array<{ product: string; qty: number }>>('lines').push({ product, qty });
});

Then('the basket has {int} line(s)', (ctx, expected: number) => {
  assert.equal(ctx.state.get<unknown[]>('lines').length, expected);
});</cb>
<p>The first argument is the <em>context</em> (see below). The values captured from the step text follow it. A step passes when it returns, or when its promise resolves. It fails when it throws.</p>

<h2>Patterns</h2>
<p>Patterns are <a href="https://github.com/cucumber/cucumber-expressions">Cucumber Expressions</a>:</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>In the pattern</th><th>Matches</th><th>You receive</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>{int}</code></td><td><code>42</code></td><td>a number</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{float}</code></td><td><code>3.5</code></td><td>a number</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{string}</code></td><td><code>"apple"</code> or <code>'apple'</code></td><td>the text without quotes</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>{word}</code></td><td><code>apple</code></td><td>a word</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>cat(s)</code></td><td><code>cat</code> or <code>cats</code></td><td>nothing</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>red/green</code></td><td>either word</td><td>nothing</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>You can use a regular expression instead. Each capture group becomes an argument.</p>
<cb>Then(/^the user is (.+)$/, (ctx, name: string) => { /* ... */ });</cb>
<p>Add your own types with <a href="parameter-types.html">parameter types</a>.</p>

<h2>The context</h2>
<p>The context is how steps share data and reach the framework.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td><code>ctx.state</code></td><td>Data for this scenario. Gone when the scenario ends. <code>get</code>, <code>set</code> and <code>getOrSet</code> are typed.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.feature</code>, <code>ctx.groups[name]</code>, <code>ctx.run</code></td><td>Wider stores for a feature, a group and the whole run.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.params</code></td><td>Values from <code>-D key=value</code> and the config <code>params</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.scenario</code></td><td>Id, name, tags, <code>meta</code>, the example row and the attempt number.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.log</code></td><td>Levelled logging: <code>ctx.log.info('...')</code>. <code>ctx.log.image()</code> attaches a screenshot.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.attach(body, mediaType, name)</code></td><td>Attach anything to the report.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.soft</code></td><td>Soft assertions: <code>check</code> and <code>run</code> record a failure and let the step continue. The scenario fails at the end.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.defer(fn)</code></td><td>Run a cleanup when the scenario ends.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.signal</code></td><td>An <code>AbortSignal</code> that fires on timeout or Ctrl+C. Pass it to APIs that accept one.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.export</code>, <code>ctx.from(id)</code></td><td>Pass values to dependent scenarios. See <a href="dependencies.html">Dependencies</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ctx.page</code>, <code>ctx.request</code>, ...</td><td>Fixtures that plugins add. See <a href="fixtures.html">Fixtures and inject()</a>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>

<h2>Step options</h2>
<cb>When('I open the report', { timeoutMs: 20_000, retry: { attempts: 3, delay: '1s' } }, async (ctx) => {
  // ...
});

When('I click {string}', { concurrent: false }, async ({ page }, label: string) => {
  await page.getByRole('button', { name: label }).click();
});</cb>
<ul>
  <li><code>timeoutMs</code>: how long the step may take.</li>
  <li><code>retry</code>: run again until it passes. A number, or <code>{ attempts, delay, backoff }</code>.</li>
  <li><code>concurrent: false</code>: this step never runs in parallel with itself. Use it for steps that drive a browser. <code>@concurrency</code> on such a step is an error.</li>
  <li><code>tags</code>: only match in scenarios whose tags satisfy the expression.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Pending and undefined steps</h2>
<p>A step with no definition is <em>undefined</em>. By default that fails the run. Print code to paste for every undefined step:</p>
<cb lang="bash">$ npx bddr snippets</cb>
<p>Use <code>--no-strict</code> if pending and undefined steps should not fail the run. If two definitions match one step, bddr reports an ambiguity instead of picking one.</p>

<h2>Repeat and retry from the feature file</h2>
<p>Tags at the end of a step line repeat or retry just that step: <code>@repeat:N</code>, <code>@retry:N</code>, <code>@delay:2s</code>, <code>@backoff:2</code>, <code>@timeout:10s</code> and <code>@concurrency:N</code>. See <a href="retries.html">Retries and flaky tests</a>.</p>
